cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, dataset, or its generated results, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Universal Atomic Model: Halo and Drip-Line Evidence Study V10.1"
type: software
version: "10.1.0"
date-released: "2026-07-12"
authors:
  - family-names: "Dabas"
    given-names: "Monty"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6948-209X"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible nuclear mass-surface evidence study evaluating externally
  annotated halo-nucleus candidates using leakage-safe same-parity
  reconstruction, threshold-sensitive drip-line classification, strict
  matched controls, expanded sensitivity analysis, deterministic reports,
  regression tests, and a reproduction certificate on a frozen
  AME2020/NUBASE2020-derived dataset.
keywords:
  - nuclear binding energy
  - halo nuclei
  - neutron drip line
  - atomic mass evaluation
  - NUBASE2020
  - nuclear mass interpolation
  - same-parity reconstruction
  - selective prediction
  - matched controls
  - reproducible research
repository-code: "https://github.com/Parveen117/Atomic-validation-public"
url: "https://github.com/Parveen117/Atomic-validation-public"
